<title>USA: U.S. March PPI energy goods prices.</title>
<headline>U.S. March PPI energy goods prices.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Labor Department reported energy components of the producer price index as follows, with comparisons (1982=100 unless stated otherwise).</p>
<p>    Percent Changes:    Seasonally Adj.  Unadjusted</p>
<p> -				 Mar    Feb    Mar97/96</p>
<p> Finished Energy Goods    -3.4   -1.2	3.5</p>
<p> -Gasoline		    -4.0   -3.1	7.6</p>
<p> -Heating Oil		 -9.9   -1.1     -2.9</p>
<p> -Residential Gas-Y	 -4.8    0.2	6.3</p>
<p>Y-Dec 1990=100.  </p>
<p>  Percent Changes:    Seasonally Adj.  Unadjusted</p>
<p> -				 Mar    Feb    Mar97/96</p>
<p> Intermed.Energy Goods    -4.6   -0.6	2.8</p>
<p> -Liq.Petroleum Gas-Z    -20.7   -7.3     12.7</p>
<p> -Jet Fuel		    -8.7    2.7     12.2</p>
<p> -Diesel Fuel		-10.7    1.6	5.3</p>
<p> -Residual Fuel-Z	  -20.4    2.3     -5.3</p>
<p>Z-Current data not seasonally adjusted.  </p>
<p>  Percent Changes:    Seasonally Adj.  Unadjusted</p>
<p> -				 Mar    Feb    Mar97/96</p>
<p> Crude Energy Materials  -19.2  -12.4	3.0</p>
<p> -Coal-Z			 3.2   -3.7	0.7</p>
<p> -Natural Gas-Z	    -29.2  -14.7	8.2</p>
<p> -Petroleum-Z		-13.4  -12.2     -2.4</p>
<p>Note-Crude energy materials include crude petroleum. Z-Current data not seasonally adjusted.</p>
</text>
